00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  my name is dianna  bartschniebs i'm based in liesman in  [Music]  portugal  [Music]  my education was in a contemporary dance  and ballet  and then i started to make a fusion with  kind of acrobatic and aerialism  and then i got an accident and i won  a wheelchair so i start dancing also  with my disability  so i find this new body  and i start recovering actually from  from my accident through dance dance  for me have this kind of special meaning  of magic state  [Music]  in my work i like to  mix normative bodies with no normative i  like to use bionic  things on stage i'm also very open  to collaborate in terms of sounds  lights space  i like the audience surrounding near  and this kind of communication between  [Music]  the performer and the audience  my body is an accident so  i feel all the bodies are kind of an  accident of society  so i try to create an idea of shock  and landscape of bodies that are  conventional and not conventional  and they are very similar in between so  you cannot understand what's the  convention  of these bodies so i try to work in this  idea  and in terms of performance i like this  idea of hypnosis  and this idea of a different time zone  from reality  i like to show the body i feel like  persons with disability not often very  often show their body  on stage i like to  show what we are and uniqueness of that  and it's  quite interesting to see that we are not  all the same  [Music]  the importance of the body is much more  important to me now  [Music]  you

